+## GLM eight concurrent streams (--parallel up to 8, TF_GLM_MULTI_WINDOW)
+
+`--parallel` 1 to 8 for GLM-5.3-Flash (`engine.py`'s `PARALLEL_MOST`, `multi_window`, `multi_decode_rows`, the
+multi-stream drafter's estimate past four streams in `multi_draft_bytes`, and the window in the startup estimate and the
+settings both ranks compare), `segments.py`'s `MAX_SEGS`, `SEGS_DEFAULT` and `seg_count` (a batched window's segment
+tables sized by the streams, four as before up to four), `verify.py`'s `BatchedVerify(segs=)`, `multi.py`'s
+`MultiDecoder.window` (the shared verify window's rows, TF_GLM_MULTI_WINDOW, 32 by default) and
+`cuda/geometry.py`'s `mla_geometry(decode_rows=)` / `MLA_DECODE_ROWS` are ported from MiaAI-Lab's
+[GLM-5.3-Flash EXL3 2x DGX Spark recipe](https://github.com/MiaAI-Lab/GLM-5.3-Flash-EXL3-2x-DGX-Sparks-TensorFold/tree/1576746)
+patch 0069-glm-eight-streams (v1.5), Apache License 2.0, Copyright 2026 MiaAI-Lab (see
+[the license text](LICENSES/Apache-2.0.txt)). Changes in the port: TF_GLM_MULTI_WINDOW defaults to 32 at every
+`--parallel` (the recipe's `config.sh` sets 64 past four requests); the main `--parallel` start line names the window
+only when it is not 32, and the AFD attention node reads TF_GLM_MULTI_WINDOW before the expert wire opens; this tree's
+8-row stream windows (`MAX_ROWS`) keep the multi-stream drafter's 64-row updates and block passes up to eight streams,
+so the estimate's activation term the recipe adds past four is 0 here. With `--parallel` at 4 or less and
+TF_GLM_MULTI_WINDOW unset, tables, buffers, estimate and calls are the ones before.
